Use only supplied learner evidence and context guidance. Identify unfamiliar cues, not presumed audience traits. Keep conflicting reviewer observations separate and narrow claims to the evidenced subgroup or setting. Flag stereotype risks and request appropriate context review before reusing a culturally specific example.
